#: build-src/appendix/glossary.md:1
msgid "Glossary"
msgstr ""

#: build-src/appendix/glossary.md:3
msgid "All definition for terms and acronyms used in this documentation."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/appendix/glossary.md:5
msgid ""
"**PGCN**: _Plateforme de Gestion de Contenu Numérisé_. Original name of "
"NumaHOP."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/appendix/glossary.md:7
msgid ""
"**OCR** : _Optical Character Recognition_. Process by which text is "
"recognized on images."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/appendix/glossary.md:9
msgid "Metadata standards and file formats"
msgstr ""

#: build-src/appendix/glossary.md:11
msgid ""
"**METS** : _Metata-Data Encoding and Transportation Standard_ An XML "
"[standard](https://www.loc.gov/standards/mets/)."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/appendix/glossary.md:13
msgid "**EAD** : _Encoded Archival Description_."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/appendix/glossary.md:15
msgid ""
"**DC** : _DublinCore_ Small Set of core metadata for bibliographic units "
"[User Guide](https://www.dublincore.org/resources/userguide/)."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/appendix/glossary.md:17
msgid ""
"**SIP** : _Submission Information Package_ A file describing a package to be "
"archived."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/appendix/glossary.md:19
msgid ""
"**AIP** : _Archival Information Package_ A file representing an archived "
"packaged."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/appendix/glossary.md:21
msgid ""
"**XSD** : _XML Schema Definition_ An XML file describing an XML format "
"allowing an XML parser to verify a file is well formed according to a "
"standard."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/appendix/glossary.md:23
msgid ""
"**MARC**: Format for bibliographic data [Spec](https://www.loc.gov/marc/"
"bibliographic/)."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/appendix/glossary.md:25
msgid "**ALTO** :  _Analyzed Layout and Text Object_."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/appendix/glossary.md:27
msgid "Protocols"
msgstr ""

#: build-src/appendix/glossary.md:29
msgid ""
"**OAI-PMH** : _Open Archives Initiative Protocol for Metadata Harvesting_ "
"[Spec](https://www.openarchives.org/OAI/openarchivesprotocol.html)."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/appendix/glossary.md:31
msgid ""
"**Z39.50** : A protocol to searching and retrieving data in databases "
"between servers over TCP/IP."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/appendix/glossary.md:33
msgid ""
"**IIIF** : A REST API for requesting documents and their images [SPEC]"
"(https://iiif.io/api/)."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/appendix/glossary.md:35
msgid "NumaHOP Vocabulary"
msgstr ""

#: build-src/appendix/glossary.md:37
msgid ""
"**Digitalization service provider**: The company(for external "
"digitalization) or service (internal digitalization) doing the "
"digitalization process."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/appendix/glossary.md:39
msgid ""
"**Document Unit**: Also referred as `Doc Unit` or `DU`; A Document or part "
"of a document for collections to be processed by NumaHOP."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/appendix/glossary.md:41
msgid ""
"**Workflow**: Steps the Document Unit takes trough NumaHOP. Can be defined "
"at the project level, or the bundle level."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/appendix/glossary.md:43
msgid "**Notice**: Bibliographic meta-datas attached to a DU."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/appendix/glossary.md:45
msgid ""
"**Condition Report**: A check of the state of the document after it was "
"manipulated during the digitalization process."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/appendix/glossary.md:47
msgid ""
"**Delivery**: The step where the digitalized documents are deposited into "
"NumaHOP and attached to the correct Document Unit."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/appendix/glossary.md:49
msgid "**Import**: The step where we create the Document Unit."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/appendix/glossary.md:51
msgid "Grouping of Document Units"
msgstr ""

#: build-src/appendix/glossary.md:52
msgid ""
"**Project**: A project is usually a set of documents to be digitalized by "
"the same provider."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/appendix/glossary.md:54
msgid ""
"**Bundle**: A physical set of Documentary Units averaging around 20 to 50 "
"documents."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/appendix/glossary.md:56
msgid ""
"**Train**: As in digitalization train. Smaller set of document for insurance "
"reason."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/appendix/glossary.md:58
msgid ""
"All sets of grouping are not necessarily useful for all use cases. For "
"smaller volume of documents in a project the train is not as useful."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/appendix/glossary.md:60
msgid "Design Pattenrn jargon"
msgstr ""

#: build-src/appendix/glossary.md:62
msgid ""
"**DTO**: _Data Transfer Object_ an object traveling between the view and the "
"controller."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/appendix/glossary.md:64
msgid "**Service**: Class containing business logic."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/appendix/glossary.md:66
msgid ""
"**Repository**: Class abstracting a storage method (database, elasticsearch "
"or file system)."
msgstr ""

#: build-src/appendix/glossary.md:68
msgid "**Mapper**: Class performing mapping from a domain object to another."
msgstr ""
